  "careCheckupsScienceTitle": "Preventive check-ups",
  "careCheckupsScienceBadge": "Prevention",
  "careCheckupsScienceQuick": "Many common conditions (high blood pressure, diabetes, some cancers) are easier to treat the earlier they're found, and they often cause no symptoms at first. This list reminds you what's due for your age and sex.",
  "careCheckupsScienceHow": "The intervals are a guide, taken from Colombia's Health Promotion and Maintenance Pathway (Resolution 3280 of 2018) and WHO recommendations. Your personal or family history may change them: adjust them to what your doctor tells you. None of this leaves your phone.",
  "careCheckupsScienceAdvice": "Tap “I've done it” with the date and we'll tell you when the next one is due. If there's a family history (bowel, breast or prostate cancer, for example), ask whether you should start earlier.",
  "careCheckupsScienceRefs": "Ministerio de Salud y Protección Social de Colombia. Resolución 3280 de 2018.\nWHO. Prevention and control of noncommunicable diseases.\nUSPSTF. Recommendations for primary care practice.",
