  "careAlcoholScienceTitle": "The standard drink",
  "careAlcoholScienceBadge": "WHO",
  "careAlcoholScienceQuick": "A standard drink has 10 g of pure alcohol: roughly a 330 ml beer, a 100 ml glass of wine or a 30 ml shot of spirits.",
  "careAlcoholScienceHow": "Alcohol provides 7 kcal per gram, worsens deep sleep even if it helps you fall asleep, raises blood pressure and, in the long run, increases the risk of several cancers. There's no completely safe amount: less is always better.",
  "careAlcoholScienceAdvice": "If you drink, leave at least two alcohol-free days a week and don't go over two drinks in a day. If you want to quit smoking or vaping, your health service can support you; cutting down already counts.",
  "careAlcoholScienceRefs": "WHO (2023). No level of alcohol consumption is safe for our health.\nEbrahim IO et al. (2013). Alcohol and sleep I: effects on normal sleep. Alcoholism: Clinical and Experimental Research.\nWHO (2024). Guideline for clinical interventions for tobacco cessation.",
