  "quitBenefitTobacco20m": "Your heart rate and blood pressure start to drop.",
  "quitBenefitTobacco12h": "The carbon monoxide in your blood returns to normal levels.",
  "quitBenefitTobacco2d": "Nerve endings recover: smell and taste improve.",
  "quitBenefitTobacco3d": "The nicotine has left your body. Cravings are usually strongest these days and start to ease from here.",
  "quitBenefitTobacco2w": "Circulation and lung function improve: walking and climbing stairs get easier.",
  "quitBenefitTobacco1m": "Coughing and shortness of breath decrease (between 1 and 9 months); the cilia in your lungs repair.",
  "quitBenefitTobacco1y": "Your extra risk of coronary heart disease is half that of someone who smokes.",
  "quitBenefitTobacco5y": "Your stroke risk can match that of someone who never smoked (between 5 and 15 years).",
  "quitBenefitTobacco10y": "Your risk of dying from lung cancer is about half what it would be if you kept smoking.",
  "quitBenefitVape20m": "Your heart rate and blood pressure start to drop.",
  "quitBenefitVape3d": "The nicotine has left your body. Withdrawal peaks and eases from here.",
  "quitBenefitVape2w": "You breathe better and circulation improves.",
  "quitBenefitVape4w": "Most nicotine withdrawal symptoms have passed (2 to 4 weeks).",
  "quitBenefitVape3m": "Cravings are much less frequent and your lungs keep recovering.",
  "quitBenefitAlcohol1d": "Your body has finished clearing the alcohol and your hydration improves.",
  "quitBenefitAlcohol3d": "The hardest part is usually between days 1 and 3; from here, less anxiety and irritability.",
  "quitBenefitAlcohol1w": "You sleep more deeply: REM sleep recovers and you wake up more rested.",
  "quitBenefitAlcohol2w": "Less heartburn and better digestion, and you've left many empty calories behind.",
  "quitBenefitAlcohol1m": "Liver fat may go down, and blood pressure and insulin sensitivity improve.",
  "quitBenefitAlcohol3m": "If the damage was mild, liver enzymes usually return to normal. More energy and better mood.",
  "quitBenefitAlcohol1y": "Your risks of high blood pressure, liver disease and several types of cancer go down.",
  "quitBenefitSugar3d": "Sweet cravings usually peak and then start to ease.",
  "quitBenefitSugar2w": "Your energy is steadier: fewer slumps after eating.",
  "quitBenefitSugar1m": "Your palate adapts: fruit and natural foods start to taste sweeter.",
  "quitBenefitSugar3m": "Very sweet things taste more intense and cravings show up much less.",
  "quitBenefitCaffeine1d": "Withdrawal starts within 12 to 24 h: a mild headache is normal and passes. Drink water.",
  "quitBenefitCaffeine2d": "Symptoms usually peak between 20 and 51 h; from here, they improve.",
  "quitBenefitCaffeine9d": "Withdrawal ends within 2 to 9 days: your energy no longer depends on a cup.",
  "quitBenefitCaffeine2w": "You fall asleep more easily and sleep more deeply.",
  "quitBenefitScreen1d": "You got back the time that used to slip away scrolling.",
  "quitBenefitScreen1w": "Many people notice they sleep better and compare their life less with others'.",
  "quitBenefitScreen3w": "Limiting social media for 3 weeks reduced loneliness and low mood in a controlled study.",
  "quitBenefitGambling1d": "A whole day in which your money stayed with you.",
  "quitBenefitGambling1w": "The urge to “win it back” starts to lose its pull.",
  "quitBenefitGambling1m": "You sleep better and anxiety about results goes down.",
  "quitBenefitGambling3m": "Cravings come less and less and your finances can breathe.",
  "quitBenefitCannabis2d": "Irritability, low appetite and poor sleep may appear: it's withdrawal and it's temporary.",
  "quitBenefitCannabis1w": "The most intense part usually passes between days 2 and 6.",
  "quitBenefitCannabis2w": "Most symptoms have eased and your mind is clearer.",
