  "bodyCatKg": "-- kg",
  "bodyCatIncluyeElMusculoEsqueleticoLiso": "Includes skeletal and smooth muscle and the water inside muscle cells. Keeping or building muscle supports your insulin sensitivity, posture and daily energy burn.",
  "bodyCatReferenciaOrientativaHombre40Del": "Rough reference (male): > 40% of total body weight.",
  "bodyCatReferenciaOrientativaMujer32Del": "Rough reference (female): > 32% of total body weight.",
  "bodyCatMasaMuscularPesoTotalMasa": "Muscle mass = Total weight − Fat mass − Bone mineral mass.",
  "bodyCatEsTodoElPesoDe": "Everything your body weighs except fat: muscle, bone, organs, blood and water. It's the main factor in how many calories you burn at rest.",
  "bodyCatEnEtapasDePerdidaDe": "While losing fat, the aim is to keep fat-free mass steady with enough protein and strength training.",
  "bodyCatLbmPeso1GrasaCorporal": "LBM = Weight × (1 − % Body fat / 100).",
  "bodyCatPorcentajeDeAguaTotalIntracelular": "Percentage of total water, inside and outside cells. Muscle holds much more water (~73%) than fat (~10%), so more lean mass naturally raises this value.",
