  "bodyCatIndiceAntropometricoImpedanciometricoAcotadoEn": "Anthropometric and impedance index on a scale of 1 to 30.",
  "bodyCatEstimaElPesoDelMineral": "Estimates the weight of bone mineral (calcium, phosphorus and structural matrix). It doesn't measure clinical bone density (DEXA), but it closely follows the development of your lean mass.",
  "bodyCatPromedioOrientativoHombreAdulto2": "Rough average (adult male): 2.5 – 3.5 kg depending on height.",
  "bodyCatPromedioOrientativoMujerAdulta1": "Rough average (adult female): 1.9 – 2.8 kg depending on height.",
  "bodyCatEstimacionLinealDerivadaDeLa": "Linear estimate derived from fat-free mass (LBM).",
  "bodyCatKcal": "-- kcal",
  "bodyCatEnergiaMinimaDiariaQueTu": "The minimum daily energy your body needs at complete rest to keep your heart beating, breathe, hold its temperature and renew cells. Your calorie goal should never go below this physiological floor.",
  "bodyCatAMayorMasaLibreDe": "The more fat-free mass (muscle) you have, the higher your daily basal metabolism.",
